# Chapter 16: Transgenic animals

=== layout: subsection

# Topic 31: GMO mosquito

=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 31: GMO mosquito

@body

- If we change mosquitoes, can we reduce the diseases they transmit?
- Anopheles transmit malaria parasites; Aedes species transmit several important arboviruses.
- Some approaches suppress the mosquito population. Others reduce pathogen transmission.
- Self-limiting transgenes, Wolbachia, and gene drives work differently. Keep them separate.

@notes

