=== layout: two-panels

# 31. Gene drive spread and cage suppression

@left

![Drive frequency and egg production by generation](assets/lect06c-set_4_tp_chapter_12_16_material/image_075.png)

@right

- Each cage began with 300 wild-type females, 150 wild-type males, and 150 GM males.
- Drive prevalence reached 100% in generations 7 and 11.
- Egg production collapsed in generations 8 and 12.
- Compare the two trajectories; the next slide enlarges them.

@notes

Source: ../old/lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 103.
